Regulatory and Implementation Notice (Informational; 2026-11-04)
========================================================================

Technical separation does not make a transfer anonymous, exempt, approved or
lawful by itself. Public names/content may identify users despite HMAC-derived
references. HMAC has no decryption key; this release stores its regional secret
in process memory, not an HSM. Ed25519 supplies signature integrity/authenticity,
not confidentiality or transport security. Hardware-attestation verification,
PDQ extraction, TMK matching and authoritative media-safety feeds are not supplied.
References to those technologies elsewhere are not claims of implementation.

Operators must assess the applicable Chinese, EU/EEA, U.S. and other requirements
for their actual entities, data flows, purposes and scale. Depending on the facts,
these can include transfer mechanisms, assessments, notices/consents, data
classification, cybersecurity, incident response, retention, individual rights,
platform duties and national-security restrictions. A filter result, pseudonym,
signature or audit of one component is not proof of overall legal compliance.
The supplied catalogs are examples; filtering does not exempt an operator from
content-related obligations or establish that prohibited content never arrives.

An EU SCC is a contract between exporter and importer; a Chinese standard
contract is between the domestic processor and overseas recipient, subject to
applicable filing rules. They are not contracts with regulators and are not the
only possible transfer routes. Assess current eligibility, exceptions and other
required safeguards. Separating databases does not itself resolve restrictions
on operational relationships or data sharing under applicable U.S. measures.

Before production activation, operators need a documented local determination
covering the proposed route and current applicable requirements. The software
checks do not verify that evidence. A separate deployment authorization process,
network isolation and operational security remain necessary integration work.
See docs/LEGAL_DEPLOYMENT.md for dated source-linked guidance and the implementation
gap matrix. This notice is not legal advice, regulatory approval, certification,
or an assurance against fines, sanctions or liability.

